{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:4b74a152cff8972d","name":"Charlatan Talent Trees","source":{"id":"source:reference-4b74a152cff8972d","title":"Charlatan Talent Trees","revision":18028,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T19:28:08Z","sha256":"287c7df3e89a8be7d77eb6fe7d041be14b3505333523bdc0c2ed5e015afdd5b6","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18028","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Charlatan%20Talent%20Trees&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-4b74a152cff8972d","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scum and Villainy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scum_and_Villainy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["At every odd-numbered level (1st, 3rd, 5th, and so on), a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Charlatan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Charlatan","referenceId":"reference:e577203c5f4dbcc8"}," gains an additional Charlatan Talent. A ",{"tag":"a","children":["Charlatan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Charlatan","referenceId":"reference:e577203c5f4dbcc8"}," may choose a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Talent"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Talent"}," from any of the following Charlatan Talent Trees they wish, but they must meet the prerequisites (if any) of the chosen Charlatan Talent. No ",{"tag":"a","children":["Talent"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Talent"}," can be selected more than once unless expressly indicated.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Core Talent Trees"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["TALENT TREE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["DESCRIPTION\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SOURCE\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Fortune Talent Tree"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortune_Talent_Tree","referenceId":"reference:5bd9c10b1af0ad71"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Many ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scoundrels"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scoundrels"}," like to gamble with destiny, putting everything on the line and trusting fate (or ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},") to bring them fortune, fame, and success.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"}]},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Disgrace Talent Tree"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Disgrace_Talent_Tree","referenceId":"reference:934cf1fece146b2a"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Scandal fouls your family name, forcing you to live among the fringes of society and teaching you that honor is overrated when victory is on the line.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Scum and Villainy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scum_and_Villainy"}]},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Trickery Talent Tree"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Trickery_Talent_Tree","referenceId":"reference:9810bb779227791d"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Charlatans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Charlatans"}," are masters of misdirection, confusion, and trickery. They owe their success in double-cross to their uncanny knack for cultivating the existing beliefs of their marks and twisting them in subtle ways to their own benefit.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Scum and Villainy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scum_and_Villainy"}]},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Provocateur Talent Tree"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Provocateur_Talent_Tree","referenceId":"reference:28d6eb32d25b79b0"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["As a provocateur, you specialize in turning your enemies against one another, giving your allies the advantage. This is accomplished through a combination of gaining an enemy's confidence, making careful use of deception, and coordinating your allies' attacks.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Legacy Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Legacy_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]}]}]}]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
